From 6ba80d232faf3c0986df2eecb4b7359baeda6244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rain Valentine <rsg000@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:25:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: port the lane differential test and the split-command
 lane tests

FastpathDifftest runs seeded random pipelines of lane-eligible commands
for one to three clients through four executors on an empty database:
the write lanes with the lane key prefetch off, the lanes with it on,
the serial-segment fallback, and the plain staged executor with lane
planning off. Every reply byte of every client and a dump of the final
dataset must be identical across the four. DIFFTEST_SEEDS, DIFFTEST_FIRST,
DIFFTEST_SEED and DIFFTEST_MAXFAIL select the seeds; the default run is
2000 seeds and takes about two seconds.

FastpathLanesTest covers the split MSET and MGET atomicity and reply order,
the serial fallback, every multi-key lane command with keys in two shards
running as a barrier, and a client's own ACL change ordering its later SET.

Both suites choose their keys at suite start from this build's table hash,
use the shared test_server_init.hpp helpers and run in one process with the
other suites, shuffled and repeated. The tests of the audit stack's
generation guards (the ACL epoch re-check, the key-observer record and the
primary's window re-check) are not ported: this branch has no such guards.
No server code is changed.

Signed-off-by: Rain Valentine <rsg000@gmail.com>
